{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Read-only change-impact analysis\n\nOperations wants to add corrected trade events to the synthetic event fixture in\n`benchmark/fixtures/T8-change-impact`.\n\nRead these files:\n\n- `change-request.md`\n- `event-normalizer.mjs`\n- `event-router.mjs`\n- `event-store.mjs`\n- `event-router.test.mjs`\n\nDo not edit, create, rename, or delete files. Do not use the network, install\ndependencies, change Git state, or start a service.\n\nReturn a memo below 1,000 words with these exact sections:\n\n## Current flow\n\nTrace normalization, duplicate detection, persistence, and publication using\nconcrete functions and files.\n\n## Required changes\n\nIdentify the smallest code and contract surfaces a future implementation must\nchange. Resolve how the original and correction should coexist in audit history\nwithout both contributing to the active result.\n\n## Failure and replay risks\n\nIdentify at least four concrete risks, including publish failure and replay\nbehavior. Separate facts in the fixture from design recommendations.\n\n## Verification plan\n\nGive focused visible and private test cases. Include idempotency, missing target,\ntrade mismatch, publish failure, and input immutability.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nGive a concise implementation sequence and state the most important decision\nthat must be frozen before coding.\n"}],"timestamp":1787542785685},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_019W37xJrweYD7EE65E9DyX1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T8-change-impact/change-request.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01MBgL4dkDgcZKgu65gP2uwJ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T8-change-impact/event-normalizer.mjs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01UVzHgktGi8Fu226ppobnXx","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T8-change-impact/event-router.mjs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_015A6TYow3xgNjkmnidZeVtQ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T8-change-impact/event-store.mjs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01D41KujzUCZXZoDPY5kBLzB","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T8-change-impact/event-router.test.mjs"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":336,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":3215,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":3552,"cost":{"input":0.00001,"output":0.016800000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0401875,"total":0.056997500000000006}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787542785727,"responseId":"gen-1787542785-2tD9ZFeBU5CeS4cRJc4u","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_019W37xJrweYD7EE65E9DyX1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Change request: corrected trade events\n\nOperations needs to accept `trade.corrected` events. A correction identifies an\nearlier accepted event by `correctsEventId`, supplies a complete replacement\npayload, and must not cause the original and replacement to be counted at the\nsame time.\n\nThe team wants a change-impact memo before implementation. The memo must explain\nthe current flow, identify the exact code and contract surfaces that would need\nto change, describe failure and replay risks, and propose focused tests. No code\nshould be changed during this task.\n\nConstraints for a future implementation:\n\n- Event IDs are globally unique.\n- Corrections can arrive after the original event has already been routed.\n- The corrected event keeps its own event ID and audit timestamp.\n- A correction for a missing event is rejected rather than held indefinitely.\n- Replaying the same correction must be idempotent.\n- The in-memory store is only a fixture; do not propose a database migration.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787542789909},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01MBgL4dkDgcZKgu65gP2uwJ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const SUPPORTED_TYPES = new Set([\"trade.captured\", \"trade.cancelled\"]);\n\nexport function normalizeEvent(value) {\n  if (!value || typeof value !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(value)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event must be an object\");\n  }\n  if (typeof value.eventId !== \"string\" || value.eventId.trim() === \"\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"eventId must be a non-empty string\");\n  }\n  if (!SUPPORTED_TYPES.has(value.type)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`unsupported event type: ${value.type}`);\n  }\n  if (typeof value.tradeId !== \"string\" || value.tradeId.trim() === \"\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"tradeId must be a non-empty string\");\n  }\n  if (!value.payload || typeof value.payload !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(value.payload)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"payload must be an object\");\n  }\n\n  return {\n    eventId: value.eventId.trim(),\n    type: value.type,\n    tradeId: value.tradeId.trim(),\n    occurredAt: new Date(value.occurredAt).toISOString(),\n    payload: structuredClone(value.payload),\n  };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787542789910},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01UVzHgktGi8Fu226ppobnXx","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { normalizeEvent } from \"./event-normalizer.mjs\";\n\nexport function createEventRouter(store, publish) {\n  if (!store || typeof store.hasEvent !== \"function\" || typeof store.save !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"store is invalid\");\n  }\n  if (typeof publish !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"publish must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  return async function routeEvent(input) {\n    const event = normalizeEvent(input);\n    if (store.hasEvent(event.eventId)) {\n      return { status: \"duplicate\", eventId: event.eventId };\n    }\n\n    store.save(event);\n    await publish(event);\n    return { status: \"accepted\", eventId: event.eventId };\n  };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787542789910},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_015A6TYow3xgNjkmnidZeVtQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export function createEventStore() {\n  const events = new Map();\n\n  return {\n    hasEvent(eventId) {\n      return events.has(eventId);\n    },\n    getEvent(eventId) {\n      const event = events.get(eventId);\n      return event ? structuredClone(event) : null;\n    },\n    save(event) {\n      events.set(event.eventId, structuredClone(event));\n    },\n    listForTrade(tradeId) {\n      return [...events.values()]\n        .filter((event) => event.tradeId === tradeId)\n        .map((event) => structuredClone(event));\n    },\n  };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787542789910},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01D41KujzUCZXZoDPY5kBLzB","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { createEventRouter } from \"./event-router.mjs\";\nimport { createEventStore } from \"./event-store.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"routes a normalized event once\", async () => {\n  const store = createEventStore();\n  const published = [];\n  const route = createEventRouter(store, async (event) => published.push(event));\n  const event = {\n    eventId: \"evt-1\",\n    type: \"trade.captured\",\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    occurredAt: \"2026-08-23T12:00:00Z\",\n    payload: { notional: 1_000_000 },\n  };\n\n  assert.deepEqual(await route(event), { status: \"accepted\", eventId: \"evt-1\" });\n  assert.deepEqual(await route(event), { status: \"duplicate\", eventId: \"evt-1\" });\n  assert.equal(published.length, 1);\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787542789910},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll keep the memo concise, aiming for under 1,000 words.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"# Change-impact memo: `trade.corrected` events\n\nFixture location: `benchmark/fixtures/T8-change-impact`. No files were modified.\n\n## Current flow\n\n**Normalization.** `normalizeEvent` in `event-normalizer.mjs` rejects non-object input, requires a non-empty `eventId` and `tradeId`, requires `type` to be in `SUPPORTED_TYPES` (`trade.captured`, `trade.cancelled` only), and requires an object `payload`. It returns a fresh object with trimmed IDs, `occurredAt` coerced via `new Date(...).toISOString()`, and a `structuredClone` of the payload, so callers' input objects are never aliased.\n\n**Duplicate detection.** `createEventRouter(store, publish)` in `event-router.mjs` returns `routeEvent(input)`. After normalization it calls `store.hasEvent(event.eventId)`; if true it returns `{ status: \"duplicate\", eventId }` without saving or publishing. Uniqueness is keyed solely on `eventId`.\n\n**Persistence.** On a new event, `store.save(event)` in `event-store.mjs` writes a `structuredClone` into a `Map` keyed by `eventId`. `getEvent` and `listForTrade` return clones, so stored state is not externally mutable. `listForTrade` returns every event for a trade with no notion of superseded/active status.\n\n**Publication.** After save, the router `await publish(event)` and returns `{ status: \"accepted\", eventId }`. Note the ordering: save happens **before** publish, and there is no rollback if publish throws. `event-router.test.mjs` covers only accept-then-duplicate and single publication.\n\n## Required changes\n\nSmallest surfaces:\n\n1. **`event-normalizer.mjs`** — add `\"trade.corrected\"` to `SUPPORTED_TYPES`; validate `correctsEventId` (non-empty string, distinct from `eventId`) when and only when `type === \"trade.corrected\"`; carry it through the normalized shape.\n2. **`event-router.mjs`** — a correction branch after the duplicate check: look up the target via `store.getEvent(correctsEventId)`; reject (`{ status: \"rejected\", reason: \"missing-target\" }` or similar) if absent; reject if `target.tradeId !== event.tradeId` (a correction must not silently move a trade); then persist and publish.\n3. **`event-store.mjs`** — the minimal contract addition is a supersession marker: e.g. `markSuperseded(eventId, byEventId)` setting `supersededBy` on the stored record, plus either an `getActiveForTrade(tradeId)` helper or documented filtering semantics. No deletion.\n4. **Result contract** — a new status value for corrections (e.g. `\"corrected\"` or `\"accepted\"` plus reason) and defined rejection statuses; `event-router.test.mjs` and any consumers of the return shape are the contract surface.\n\n**Audit coexistence.** Keep both events in the store forever: the original stays under its own `eventId` and timestamp with a `supersededBy: <correctionEventId>` annotation; the correction is a first-class event with its own `eventId`, `occurredAt`, and a `correctsEventId` pointer. \"Active\" reads filter out superseded events (`listForTrade` remains full audit history; a new active-view accessor excludes records with `supersededBy` set). This satisfies the constraints that the correction keeps its own ID/timestamp and that the two never count simultaneously, without a migration — the fixture Map already supports per-record annotation.\n\n## Failure and replay risks\n\nFacts observable in the fixture:\n\n1. **Publish failure after save (fact).** The router saves before `await publish(event)`. If `publish` throws, the event is persisted but never published, and any retry with the same `eventId` returns `duplicate` without republishing — a permanently unpublished-but-stored event. For corrections this is worse: the target could be marked superseded while downstream systems never hear about it, unless the mark is deferred until publish succeeds (design choice, see below).\n2. **Replay is ID-based only (fact).** Idempotency is keyed on `eventId`. Replaying the same correction event is naturally idempotent (returns `duplicate`), which meets the constraint — but only if `markSuperseded` is itself idempotent and applied before/atomically with the duplicate short-circuit path never re-running side effects.\n3. **Out-of-order and missing targets (fact + requirement).** Corrections can arrive after routing of the original, but the fixture has no buffering; per the change request a correction with no stored target must be rejected, not queued. Risk: legitimate corrections racing ahead of their originals during a replay of an event stream will be rejected; replay order must preserve original-before-correction.\n4. **Correction chains and conflicts (design risk).** Two different corrections targeting the same original, or a correction of a correction, are unspecified. Recommendation: last-accepted correction wins by marking the prior correction superseded too, and correcting an already-superseded event should be an explicit decision (reject or re-point).\n5. **Semantic duplicates (design risk).** A resent correction with a *new* `eventId` but the same `correctsEventId` bypasses ID-based dedupe and would double-supersede. Recommendation: treat as a new correction (chain) and document it; do not attempt payload-hash dedupe in the fixture.\n6. **Cancelled-trade corrections (design risk).** Correcting a `trade.cancelled` or correcting an event on a cancelled trade is undefined and should be resolved in the contract.\n\nRecommendation vs. fact summary: 1–3 are grounded directly in fixture code and the change request; 4–6 are design recommendations for gaps the fixture does not constrain.\n\n## Verification plan\n\nVisible tests (extend `event-router.test.mjs`):\n\n- **Happy path:** route original, route correction → correction accepted; active view for the trade contains only the correction; audit list contains both; original shows `supersededBy`.\n- **Idempotency:** route the same correction twice → second returns `duplicate`; publish called once; supersession state unchanged.\n- **Missing target:** correction whose `correctsEventId` was never stored → rejected, nothing saved, nothing published.\n- **Trade mismatch:** correction with a `tradeId` different from the target's → rejected.\n\nPrivate tests:\n\n- **Publish failure:** `publish` throws on the correction → assert whether the original remains active (i.e., supersession not applied, or applied per the frozen decision) and that a retry behaves deterministically; also assert the existing save-before-publish gap for plain events.\n- **Input immutability:** freeze/snapshot the caller's input object and payload; assert router and store never mutate them (clone semantics from `normalizeEvent` and `save` hold for the new type).\n- **Self-correction:** `correctsEventId === eventId` rejected at normalization.\n- **Correction-of-correction / competing corrections:** assert the frozen chain policy.\n- **Normalization negatives:** missing/blank `correctsEventId` on `trade.corrected`; `correctsEventId` present on non-correction types (define: ignored or rejected).\n\n## Recommendation\n\nSequence: (1) freeze the contract decisions below; (2) extend `normalizeEvent` + unit tests; (3) add store supersession API + tests; (4) add the router correction branch with reject paths; (5) add publish-failure and replay tests; (6) update result-status documentation.\n\n**Decision to freeze first:** the atomicity/ordering of supersession versus publish — specifically whether the original is marked superseded before or only after `publish` succeeds, and what a retry after a publish failure must do. Every failure and replay test above depends on that single choice, so it must be fixed before any code is written."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":2623,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":5126,"reasoning":16,"totalTokens":7751,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.13115000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.064075,"total":0.195245}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787542789911,"responseId":"gen-1787542789-fxdepU5o2Yf6hyTQoA7c","rawStopReason":"stop"}],"willRetry":false}
